// Check why nrp.s > 0.5 && nPos[0] > 0.2 triggered during RELEASE_AND_ROLL when falling at x ~ 10m, y ~ 12m!
// Wait: at x = 10m, y = 12m (in mid-air 8m away from the ramp!), why was dRamp < 0.02?!
// Because dRamp = (nPos[0] - nrp.x) * nrp.nx + (nPos[1] - nrp.y) * nrp.ny is a SIGNED projection!
// When the car is on the overhanging/inside side, nrp.nx is NEGATIVE (-0.91), so moving to the left (-X, away from the ramp) makes (nPos[0] - nrp.x) * nrp.nx POSITIVE (+8m)!
